```
You are creating a [[Data type]]
A structure is a [[Compound type]]

ex:
```c++
struct Student{
	int student_id;
	double GPA;
	bool part_time;
}
int main(){
	Student jones;
	//or
	Student jane = {12344, 3.7, false}
	
	jones.student_id = 12344;
	jones.GPA = 3.7;
	jones.part_time = false;
	
	return 0;
}
```
You **CAN**
- pass a structure to a function
- compare (jane.GPA == jones.GPA)
- return a structure from a function
- Assign an object to another object (jones = jane)

You **CANNOT** 
- compare structures with logical operators. ex (jane == jones)

A structure is a type definition, NOT a variable declaration.

***Functions and Structures as parameters***
Pass by value by default, but pass by refference works as well.
```C++
Student read_student(){

	Student student;
	...
	return student;
}
```

